// Signing — what the repository ships, and the door to a per-machine override.
//
// OBJEKAT signs AD HOC with NO development team on purpose, so that anyone can
// build it with no Apple account: a team ID committed into project.pbxproj
// would stop every contributor at the signing step (see CLAUDE.md).
//
// The cost of an ad-hoc signature is that the designated requirement IS the
// cdhash of that exact binary, and TCC keys its grants to the requirement — so
// macOS asks for Desktop / Documents access again after EVERY rebuild. Whoever
// is tired of that signs locally with their own identity, in
// Signing.local.xcconfig, which .gitignore keeps out of the repository. The
// optional include below is silent when that file is absent, which is the
// state every clone arrives in.
//
// These settings live here and NOT in project.pbxproj: a value set on the
// target wins over an xcconfig, so the local override would never be read.
// If Xcode writes them back into the target (it does as soon as you touch
// Signing & Capabilities), take them out again rather than committing them.

CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER =

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
